# Runtime versions the measurements are pinned to.
#
# setup.sh enforces these and refuses to prepare a machine that cannot meet them,
# so that every environment records the same runtime in its result files. The
# library versions are pinned separately and per language: node/package-lock.json,
# go/go.sum and python/requirements.txt.
#
# Why pin the runtime at all: the interpreter itself moves these benchmarks by
# well under the run-to-run spread, so this is not about speed. It is about the
# result files being comparable -- a measurement that records a different runtime
# than another cannot be placed beside it, and the papers' environment table has
# to state one version per environment.
#
# To move a pin: change it here, re-run ./setup.sh on every measurement machine,
# re-measure all of them, and update the environment table. Do not change it for
# one machine only.
#
# These values were chosen so that three of the four environments already met them
# and only one had to move, which is why they are not simply the newest releases:
#
#   env            was                                   needs
#   A EPYC 7763    node v24.18.0 go1.22.2  py 3.12.3     go patch only
#   B Celeron      node v22.22.1 go1.26.0  py 3.14.4     node, go and python
#   C M1 Ultra     node v24.18.0 go1.22.12 py 3.12.15    nothing
#   D Xeon E5645   node v24.18.0 go1.22.12 py 3.12.15    nothing
#
# Aligning all four is what lets a difference between any two of them be attributed
# to the hardware. Until the 2026-10-23 round, that held only among A, C and D.

# Exact version. node --version must print v$NODE_VERSION.
NODE_VERSION=24.18.0

# Exact version, enforced through GOTOOLCHAIN, which makes any Go 1.21 or newer
# fetch and use precisely this toolchain. The version recorded in the result
# files is the toolchain that compiled go/vc-bench, so this fixes that value.
GO_VERSION=1.22.12

# Minor version. CPython patch releases are not reliably installable everywhere,
# so the patch is reported rather than enforced; the dependency versions, which
# are what actually matter here, are pinned exactly in python/requirements.txt.
PYTHON_MINOR=3.12
